	(text "Rp = 10 kΩ on CC1/CC2: USB-C source advertising 3 A.\nThe Pi 5 runs at full power with PSU_MAX_CURRENT=5000\n(EEPROM) and usb_max_current_enable=1 (config.txt).\nShort USB-C ↔ USB-C cable (≈ 15 cm); right-angle plug into J702\n(the main board has a notch under the plug overmold)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 254 109.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "815f4e7c-5c26-542a-99ed-6ae4f380d5ac")
	)
	(text "NOTES\n• J701: 2×6 shrouded box header, straight 12-way IDC ribbon\n  (2×6 female IDC on both ends) to Pi header pins 1–12.\n• Pi config.txt:\n    dtparam=uart0=on                  (GPIO14/15)\n    dtoverlay=gpio-shutdown           (GPIO3, active low)\n    dtoverlay=gpio-poweroff,gpiopin=4,timeout_ms=5000\n    usb_max_current_enable=1\n• Pi EEPROM: PSU_MAX_CURRENT=5000.\n• gpio-poweroff on the Pi 5 pulses (active 100 ms, inactive\n  100 ms, active): the ESP32 latches the FIRST rising edge.\n• Power sequence: ESP32 sends SHUTDOWN over UART (or pulls\n  GPIO3 low through Q701), waits for PI_PWROFF, waits 300 ms\n  and then switches the 5 V buck off (PI_PWR_OFF, sheet 3)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 254 152.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "56093c80-c526-5ce6-8ec7-ba2036a3878f")
	)
